# Privacy remediation working files must never be committed —
# they contain the private tokens they exist to remove.
.sanitize-map.txt
# .privacy-local — the operator's own privacy denylist: the private TLDs and
# hostnames the guard matches EXACTLY. It must never be committed; publishing it
# would publish the naming scheme the guard exists to keep out of this repo.
#
# The content-scanning guards do NOT catch it, which is why this line matters:
# they match hostname SHAPE (label.tld) and this file holds bare TLDs, so it
# reads clean to both the pre-commit hook and CI. This ignore line is the only
# thing keeping it out — tests/unit/test_no_private_infrastructure.py asserts
# that it still works.
.privacy-local
